From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Widen license-files to cover the bundled OpenSSL notice

`license-files = ["LICENSE"]` is an explicit PEP 639 list, so it has no
default `LICEN[CS]E*` glob behind it: a `LICENSE.openssl` dropped at the
project root to cover the OpenSSL shared library `auditwheel repair`
vendors into the wheel (dynamically linked from the build image, since
the extension is built with `--static-openssl=False` there) is silently
ignored. Widening the list picks it up with no other packaging change.

Upstream's own wheels (built with `--static-ssl` against a statically
linked, from-source OpenSSL baked into their own manylinux_2_34 image)
carry no equivalent gap, since nothing is dynamically vendored there;
this only matters for a build that links the image's OpenSSL instead.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [only relevant to a build that dynamically links the host image's OpenSSL instead of upstream's own statically-linked, from-source one]
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 421dbd6..896b3d2 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ dynamic = ["version"]
 description = "Memgraph database adapter for Python language"
 requires-python = ">=3.9"
 license = "Apache-2.0"
-license-files = ["LICENSE"]
+license-files = ["LICENSE", "LICENSE.openssl"]
 readme = { file = "README_PYPI.md", content-type = "text/markdown" }

 authors = [{ name = "Colin Barry", email = "colin.barry@memgraph.io" }]
--
2.43.0
